{"abstract":[{"text":"The nontrivial strongly connected components: the ones that contain a cycle, which are the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"components of two or more vertices and the single vertices with a self-loop. A vertex is in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one exactly when it lies on a cycle, and two vertices share one exactly when a cycle passes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through both.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/nontrivialstronglyconnectedcomponents()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"ArraySlice","preciseIdentifier":"s:s10ArraySliceV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex"},{"text":">]","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Tarjan’s algorithm, one pass: a self-loop is noticed while the search reads the vertex’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"successors.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The components are those of ","type":"text"},{"code":"stronglyConnectedComponents()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" without the trivial ones, in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same order, a reverse topological order: every path between two of them goes from a later","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one to an earlier one. Each lists its vertices in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order. Empty exactly when the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"graph is acyclic. Each is a slice of one shared array, as in ","type":"text"},{"code":"attractingComponents()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indices do not start at 0.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each component’s first vertex is its earliest in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so one sort by that vertex’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"position puts the components in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order, O(C log C) for C components. On a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"StableDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", where positions are insertion order:"}]},{"code":["let inInsertionOrder = graph.nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()","    .sorted { graph.vertexPosition(of: $0.first!) < graph.vertexPosition(of: $1.first!) }"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(V + E)."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Complexity"}]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"]]},"metadata":{"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","symbolKind":"method","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P12ConnectivityE37non